# Styling & theme

- Prefer **Tailwind utility classes** for component styling.
- Global CSS is allowed when it provides **cross-cutting behavior** (theme variables, animations, reusable utilities) and should live in `src/index.css`.

## Dark mode

- Dark mode is toggled by adding/removing the `dark` class on `document.documentElement`.
- When adding UI colors, prefer `dark:` variants instead of duplicating components.
- Reuse existing theme tokens where possible:
  - `#f1f5f9` (light surface/background)
  - `#162125` (dark background / primary ink)
  - `#3c3f40` (muted dark surface already used in the UI)

## Inline styles

- Avoid inline styles **except** for setting CSS variables or motion effects (e.g., `el.style.setProperty("--rx", ...)`).
